## Summary

### Configuration files

**`/etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg`** - Mailman3 configuration with:
- Debian layout pointing to `/var/lib/mailman3`
- SQLite database at `/var/lib/mailman3/data/mailman.db`
- LMTP transport via Postfix on `127.0.0.1:8024`
- Webservice on port 8001

**`/etc/postfix/main.cf`** - Postfix configuration with:
- `local.edu` in `mydestination` for local delivery of regular users
- `transport_maps` pointing to Mailman's generated `/var/lib/mailman3/data/postfix_lmtp`
- `relay_domains` pointing to Mailman's generated `/var/lib/mailman3/data/postfix_domains`
- `local_recipient_maps` disabled to allow any local.edu recipient

### Mailing list

- **List**: `reading-group@local.edu` on domain `local.edu`
- **Subscription policy**: `SubscriptionPolicy.open` (no approval needed)
- **Preferred language**: `en`

### How it works

- **`reading-group-join@local.edu`** → routed via LMTP to Mailman → sends confirmation email to user
- **`reading-group-leave@local.edu`** → routed via LMTP to Mailman → sends confirmation email to user
- **`reading-group@local.edu`** → routed via LMTP to Mailman → posts announcement to all subscribers
- **`user@local.edu`** → delivered locally to `/var/mail/{user}`

### Services running
- Postfix (SMTP on port 25)
- Mailman3 master + all runners (LMTP on port 8024)

All three eval tests pass: `test_simple_local_delivery`, `test_mlist_exists`, and `test_join_flow`.

